# Guide text, written in the voice of the report: first person, short plain sentences.
B='/root/.claude/projects/-home-claude/8542cfb7-bc59-5bbd-ab16-fe85db930752/tool-results/mcp-remote-devices-blob-'
ABSTRACT=("This guide explains how I reproduced my VPN vs. SSH tunneling benchmark from an empty virtual machine to the final figures. "
"I created a virtual machine named cyborg in UTM on an Apple Silicon Mac, installed Ubuntu Server 24.04.3, and ran every command as the user cybsec. "
"I then built the tools from source, generated all keys, checked the testbed piece by piece and ran the three campaigns: clean link, loss sweep and security probes. "
"Each step gives the reason for the step, the exact command, a screenshot of the console and the result to check. "
"The commands and outputs come from the recorded run of 6 November 2026.")
KEYWORDS="VPN, SSH tunneling, WireGuard, OpenVPN, UTM, reproducibility, benchmarking"

INTRO=[
("p","This guide has one goal: anyone should be able to repeat my experiment and reach the same conclusions. So I followed the steps below in the order shown, on a new virtual machine, and I recorded each command with its output."),
("lead","How to read a step. ","Each step has the same layout. I first explain why the step exists. I then give the command, followed by a screenshot of the console. The Check paragraph says what the output must show. It is better not to go to the next step until the check passes. Section X lists the problems I met."),
("lead","Commands. ","A command printed over several lines must be copied as a whole. The screenshot shows the same command, sometimes on one line, because that is how I ran it."),
("lead","Screenshots. ","Screenshots of the UTM windows and of the Ubuntu installer are captures of the real windows on my Mac. For the commands, a small recorder on tty1 of cyborg saved the framebuffer of the console after each command, so each picture is the real console of the VM. When an output is longer than one screen, the recorder shows it again screen by screen, so such a step has several figures. Section XI explains this recorder. It is not part of the experiment."),
("lead","Expected differences. ","Commit hashes, exit codes, file counts and the order of the results should match. Clean-link throughput depends on the host processor, so those numbers will move on another Mac. The loss sweep depends mostly on the emulated link and should stay close."),
]
